wayland-server: let the server's loopers be when the team exits

The add-on's loopers (the Wayland looper, the toplevels' windows, the
application looper it makes) keep running on their threads while exit() runs
libbe's static destructors (the token space, the looper list, the roster). A
message handled then used that destroyed state: a client that exits right
after destroying its toplevel (Photocraft's error exit; closing it) had the
window quit and delete itself meanwhile — "bogus pointer (double free?)" in
BTokenSpace::RemoveToken from ~BWindow, or "looper must be locked before
proceeding". (Since wl_ips_haiku_surface_view runs a window before it is
shown, every such window quits; a test client hit it in 4 exits of 15.)

An exit handler, registered when the server starts (after libbe's static
objects were made, so it runs before their destructors; with the add-on's
DSO handle, so unloading it runs it too), lets the server handle the
requests sent so far, waits (at most 1 s) for the threads of the destroyed
toplevels' windows to end, then locks the Wayland looper, every remaining
window and its own application looper (with timeouts) and keeps them locked:
their threads wait until the team's exit ends them.

